--TEST--
A static call or a static property on a class that is not declared, or a static member a declared class does not have, reports once, and using the result reports nothing — `rule:types/one-mistake-reports-once`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Shop {
    public static int $count = 0;

    // `Gone` is not declared. Each `Gone` written here gives one error, and
    // using each result as a `string` gives none.
    public static function label(): string {
        string $made = Gone::make();
        string $total = Gone::$total;
        return Gone::label();
    }

    // `Shop` has no method `nothing` and no static property `missing`.
    // Each gives one error, and returning the result gives none.
    public static function title(): string {
        string $text = Shop::nothing();
        return Shop::$missing;
    }
}
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0303]: `Gone` is not declared
  --> %s:8:24
  |
8 |         string $made = Gone::make();
  |                        ^^^^ no matching declaration

error[E0303]: `Gone` is not declared
  --> %s:9:25
  |
9 |         string $total = Gone::$total;
  |                         ^^^^ no matching declaration

error[E0303]: `Gone` is not declared
   --> %s:10:16
   |
10 |         return Gone::label();
   |                ^^^^ no matching declaration

error[E0309]: `Shop` has no method named `nothing`
   --> %s:16:24
   |
16 |         string $text = Shop::nothing();
   |                        ^^^^ referenced here

error[E0309]: `Shop` has no static property named `missing`
   --> %s:17:16
   |
17 |         return Shop::$missing;
   |                ^^^^ referenced here

error: aborting due to 5 errors
